; ============================================================ ; round nought is AddRoundKey alone
>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   ; the next round key comes off the front of the
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                       ; schedule buffer
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=98
                                                               ; THE ROUND KEY CONVEYOR  one round key taken off the
                                                               ; front of the schedule buffer  which is two hundred
                                                               ; and eight cells  and the whole buffer slid up to meet
                                                               ; the next one;
;
                                                               ; THE NAME CARRIES THE BUFFER LENGTH  as
                                                               ; keccak/sponge136 and sponge168 do and for the same
                                                               ; reason: the length is not an offset  it is the NUMBER
                                                               ; OF MOVES  so it is different text and not the same
                                                               ; text at a different base; the other AES key size
                                                               ; wants a buffer of its own length  so it has a pair of
                                                               ; its own;
;
                                                               ; THIS IS THE OTHER HALF OF THE STORED SCHEDULE DESIGN;
                                                               ; its sibling puts a word on the tail as the schedule
                                                               ; is made  and this takes sixteen bytes off the head as
                                                               ; the cipher runs; Between them no round key is ever
                                                               ; addressed by a computed offset  which is the
                                                               ; library's conveyor rule and the reason an AES_256
                                                               ; cipher is the same text as an AES_128 one with a
                                                               ; different count;
;
                                                               ; A MOVE AND NOT A COPY  in both halves; the round key
                                                               ; cells are SPENT by AddRoundKey  which exclusive ors
                                                               ; the key into the state and empties it  so the buffer
                                                               ; hands its head over rather than lending it; The entry
                                                               ; contract below claims those sixteen cells are already
                                                               ; clear  which is the cheap guard against the copy
                                                               ; where a move belonged: a copy into an occupied cell
                                                               ; ADDS  and the answer is wrong somewhere far away;
;
                                                               ; TWO HUNDRED AND EIGHT MOVES A TURN  sixteen to take
                                                               ; the key and one hundred and ninety two to close the
                                                               ; gap  and a cipher turns it once per round; It is the
                                                               ; same arithmetic the appending half does from the
                                                               ; other end  and against a round of AES it is not
                                                               ; measurable;
;
                                                               ; THE TAIL EMPTIES AS THE CONVEYOR RUNS; after the
                                                               ; slide the top sixteen cells hold nothing  because the
                                                               ; slide moved out of them and nothing moved in; The
                                                               ; exit contract says so  and that is what would catch a
                                                               ; slide whose count was one word short;
;
                                                               ; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset
                                                               ; resolves them;
;
                                                               ; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero  which IS
                                                               ; the round key cell)
;   @0x000:0x00f  round key{16}  clear on entry  full on exit
;   @0x322:0x3f1  the schedule buffer{208}  shorter by a round key on exit
;
